From 929bf61365e0d8f06a254a1710da025da88425a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fabien Danieau <fabien.danieau@pollen-robotics.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:48:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: rk3566: radxa's Zero 3W (AIC8800DS2)
 device tree

Taken verbatim from radxa/kernel at 270a678f8364 (linux-6.1-stan-rkr4.1):
rk3566-radxa-zero-3w-aic8800ds2.dts, and rk3566-radxa-zero3.dtsi in place
of this tree's own. Armbian describes the board with a different .dtsi
(no rk3568-linux.dtsi, pmuio2 at 3.3 V instead of 1.8 V, ~300 lines of
other differences); this keeps the description that microduck has run
on the board.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [configuration]
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/Makefile         |   1 +
 .../rk3566-radxa-zero-3w-aic8800ds2.dts       | 142 +++++++++
 .../boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-radxa-zero3.dtsi | 288 ++++++++----------
 3 files changed, 267 insertions(+), 164 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-radxa-zero-3w-aic8800ds2.dts

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/Makefile b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/Makefile
